---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import HorizontalCard from "../components/HorizontalCard.astro";
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import createSlug from "../lib/createSlug"

const posts = (await getCollection("blog")).sort((a, b) => b.data.pubDate.valueOf() - a.data.pubDate.valueOf());

const last_posts = posts.slice(0, 3);
---

<BaseLayout sideBarActiveItemID="home">
  <div class="pb-12 mt-5">
    <div class="text-4xl font-bold">Sen Jia</div>
    <div class="text-2xl py-3 font-bold">Machine Learning Enthusiast</div>
    <div class="py-2">
      <text class="text-xl">
      I’m Sen Jia, an Applied Researcher 2 at eBay Toronto. Our Focus Category Science team supports a wide range of categories, from collectibles and fashion to parts & accessories, and our research spans both computer vision and natural language processing. As a general C2C platform, eBay’s business is remarkably broad.
      Before joining eBay, I was an AI Research Scientist at LG Electronics’ Toronto AI Lab, where our research on topics such as face recognition and scene graph understanding led to six patent filings.

      Earlier, I was a postdoctoral fellow at the VIP Lab, University of Waterloo (October 2020 to June 2021). 
      From 2018 to 2020, I worked at the Ryerson Vision Lab under the supervision of Prof. Neil Bruce. 
      Before that, I was a research associate in data science at the University of Bristol, where I explored weakly supervised web data for computer vision tasks. 
      I received my PhD from the same university under the supervision of Prof. Nello Cristianini.
      My research interests cover machine learning and computer vision. 
        <div class="font-bold">
        Feel free to browse my github projects and publications, you might find something interesting.
        </div>
        
      </text>
    </div>
    <div class="text-2xl py-3 font-bold">Service</div>
    <div class="py-2">
      <text class="text-xl">
      I learn new CS technologies from talented people all over the world, and I contribute back to the community by serving as a reviewer for: 
      AAAI2027, ICLR2027, CVPR2026, ICLR2026, AAAI2026, ACMMM2025, Neurips2025, ICML2025, ICLR2025, AAAI2025,
      Neurips2024, ICLR2024, 
      Neurips2023, Neurips2022, ICPR2022, Neurips2021, ICCV2021, ICIP 2021, IJCV, Signal Processing Letters, ICIAP2017.
      </text>
    </div>
